Third-party datasets
================================================================================

MemTuner does NOT redistribute any third-party dataset. All datasets are
downloaded at run time from their original sources and remain under their
original licenses. Using MemTuner with a dataset means you accept that
dataset's terms. We gratefully acknowledge the authors:

- LoCoMo — Snap Research (CC BY-NC 4.0)
  https://github.com/snap-research/locomo
  Maharana et al., "Evaluating Very Long-Term Conversational Memory of LLM
  Agents", ACL 2024.

- LongMemEval — Wu et al. (MIT)
  https://github.com/xiaowu0162/LongMemEval

- SQuAD 2.0 — Stanford NLP (CC BY-SA 4.0)
  https://rajpurkar.github.io/SQuAD-explorer/
  Rajpurkar et al., "Know What You Don't Know", ACL 2018.

- CoQA — Stanford NLP (mixed component licenses; see source)
  https://stanfordnlp.github.io/coqa/
  Reddy, Chen, Manning, TACL 2019.

- HotpotQA — Yang et al. (CC BY-SA 4.0)
  https://hotpotqa.github.io/

- PersonaChat — Facebook AI Research (see source terms)
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/bavard/personachat_truecased
  Zhang et al., "Personalizing Dialogue Agents", ACL 2018.

- FEVER — Thorne et al. (annotations CC BY-SA 3.0; Wikipedia-derived)
  https://fever.ai/

- MS MARCO — Microsoft (non-commercial research terms; see source)
  https://microsoft.github.io/msmarco/

- MultiWOZ — Budzianowski et al. (MIT)
  https://github.com/budzianowski/multiwoz

- NarrativeQA — DeepMind (repository Apache 2.0; underlying texts from
